Satori Mountain is located on the southern end of [[Hyrule Ridge]]. Many [[Ore Deposit]]s, [[Rare Ore Deposit]]s, and [[Luminous Stone Deposit]]s appear throughout the Mountain. On top of the Mountain is a [[Cherry-Blossom Tree]] known as [[Mother Tree]], which sits beside a small pond. [[Rutile Lake]] also rests on Satori Mountain's western foothills, and [[Mogg Latan Shrine]] can be found near its peak. Despite the Mountain's points of interest, travelers rarely make the journey to visit it.<ref name="CaC 254"/>

[[File:BotW Satori Mountain Lord of the Mountain.png|thumb|right|320px|alt= An aerial view of Satori Mountain's summit.|The Lord of the Mountain on Satori Mountain from {{BotW|-}}]]
Occasionally, the top of Satori Mountain will glow green. During this time, the [[Lord of the Mountain]] and a group of [[Blupee]]s will appear near Mother Tree.<ref name="CaC 254"/> A variety of [[Creature]]s will also appear on Satori Mountain and in Rutile Lake, which is supposedly a result of being called there by the Lord.<ref name="CaC 254"/><ref name="BotW Botrick"/><ref name="BotW Botrick 2"/> The [[Stal]]s that are usually present on the Mountain will remain dormant during this night. However, if [[Link]] disturbs the Lord of the Mountain, it will flee, which causes the green light to fade and all of the Creatures visiting the Mountain to vanish.<ref name="CaC 254"/><ref name="CaC 157"/>

In the past, [[Quince]] ventured to Satori Mountain, hoping to hunt the Creatures that gather there and sell their [[Meat]].<ref name="BotW Quince"/> While there, he met a [[Hylian Retriever]] puppy, [[Satty]], who he gave some of his jerky to.<ref name="BotW Quince 2"/> After Quince fell asleep, he awoke to the Lord of the Mountain nearby, which began to charge at him.<ref name="BotW Quince 3"/> However, he was saved by Satty, who jumped between him and the Lord.<ref name="BotW Quince 4"/> When the Lord of the Mountain recoiled, Quince took the opportunity to grab Satty and flee from Satori Mountain.<ref name="BotW Quince 5"/>

As part of the "[[EX Ancient Horse Rumors]]" [[Side Quest]], which is exclusive to {{TCB}} [[Downloadable Content]] pack, Link reads the ''[[Super Rumor Mill V3]]'' at [[Highland Stable]].<ref name="BotW Adventure Log"/> The [[Book]] details rumors about [[Ancient Horse Gear]], claiming that the [[Ancient Bridle]] can be found underneath a cherry blossom Tree on a mountain.<ref name="BotW Super Rumor Mill V3"/> Near Mother Tree on Satori Mountain, Link will find a [[Hidden Chest]] embedded in the ground. Using [[Magnesis]], he can free the Chest, which contains the Ancient Bridle.<ref name="BotW Adventure Log 2"/>

